WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.730
Another segment that we love to do on this show,

2
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.630
which I can honestly say

3
00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.790
today feels like such a luxury

4
00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:08.890
and a privilege

5
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.851
is of course our food news.

6
00:00:12.851 --> 00:00:16.600
(cheering and applause)

7
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.910
There is an LA institution at this desk today.

8
00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.180
This hot dog dynasty has been serving

9
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.620
Hollywood hot dogs since 1939.

10
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.240
And it is still going strong

11
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.930
on the corner of La Brea and Melrose.

12
00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.610
I am honored

13
00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:36.145
as someone who grew up in 1975,

14
00:00:36.145 --> 00:00:40.720
right around the corner from Pink's hot dogs,

15
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.382
from Pink is Gloria and Beverly Pink.

16
00:00:44.382 --> 00:00:46.632
(Applause)

17
00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:49.120
Oh my god!

18
00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:49.953
What?

19
00:00:49.953 --> 00:00:50.786
We have

20
00:00:50.786 --> 00:00:51.619
Whoa!

21
00:00:51.619 --> 00:00:53.570
Those are some really big wieners.

22
00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.780
This is our newest, most favorite hot dog.

23
00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:00.325
It's the Drew's News dog and it's officially on the menu.

24
00:01:00.325 --> 00:01:04.710
We're gonna have a Drew's News hot dog on our menu

25
00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:05.562
at Pink's.

26
00:01:05.562 --> 00:01:08.010
I-- First of all, I can't believe

27
00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:12.240 line:15%
that we get to be a part of the institution for Pink's.

28
00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.200 line:15%
I mean, I was, first of all,

29
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.620 line:15%
the history is so fascinating.

30
00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.221 line:15%
Your family migrated from Russia.

31
00:01:19.221 --> 00:01:20.800
Romania and Russia.

32
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.280
Romania and Russia,

33
00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.700
opened up the hot dog stand as a cart.

34
00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:25.533
Yes.

35
00:01:25.533 --> 00:01:26.540
It was a pushcart

36
00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:29.650
and they were lucky in those days to serve 50 a day.

37
00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:31.700
Today, we serve about 2000 dogs a day.

38
00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:32.860
Wow! I was just going to ask

39
00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.690
82 years in business, how do you do it?

40
00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:36.860
You do it by selling 2000 hotdogs a day.

41
00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:37.890
That's right. That's right.

42
00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:39.410
And we are humbled and honored

43
00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:41.870
that people will wait in line for those dogs.

44
00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:44.500
Right? Because it is an iconic institution

45
00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.021
and Michelle Obama has come there.

46
00:01:46.021 --> 00:01:49.240
Yes! That was a funny story because we were,

47
00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:50.480
actually Beverly and I were there

48
00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.270 line:15%
because Japanese TV was showing up

49
00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:53.150 line:15%
to talk about Pink's

50
00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:54.180 line:15%
and somebody came up to me

51
00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.367 line:15%
and showed me his credentials.

52
00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:58.026 line:15%
They were the secret service.

53
00:01:58.026 --> 00:02:00.650
They said, somebody very important is going to be here

54
00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:01.840
in about 20 minutes.

55
00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:02.760
And we said, who is it?

56
00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.250
And they said, if you live on this planet,

57
00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:05.320
you'll know who it is.

58
00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:07.700
And it was Michelle Obama and her daughters and her mother.

59
00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.970
And then Bruce Willis proposed to Demi Moore there.

60
00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:11.930
Exactly.

61
00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:12.881
Really? - Exactly.

62
00:02:12.881 --> 00:02:13.714
Is that fun?

63
00:02:13.714 --> 00:02:16.060
It hit all the trade papers. Yeah.

64
00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:17.280
And another one,

65
00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.060
Michael J. Fox got his call for family ties

66
00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:22.010
on the payphone that was in front of Pink's

67
00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:22.930
For reals?

68
00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:25.180
He used to hang out so much at Pink's

69
00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:26.930
that he referred to Pink's as his office.

70
00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:29.270
And got the call to be Alex P. Keaton

71
00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:30.103
right then and there.

72
00:02:30.103 --> 00:02:30.936
Exactly.

73
00:02:30.936 --> 00:02:32.447
Yeah, that's a legendary scale. - How cool is that?

74
00:02:32.447 --> 00:02:33.680
The P stands for Pink's.

75
00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:35.619
That's right! Alex Pink's Keaton

76
00:02:35.619 --> 00:02:36.950
(laughs) Right, right.

77
00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:39.290
Can I just ask what's on a Drew's news hot dog?

78
00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:42.049
Yes, this is our giant 12 inch jalapeno dog

79
00:02:42.049 --> 00:02:43.470
filled with jalapeno.

80
00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.440
So it got a kick of, a little bit of a kick.

81
00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:46.273
Just like the news.

82
00:02:46.273 --> 00:02:49.060
Mustard, onions, our famous Pink's chili,

83
00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:50.979
shredded, cheddar cheese, and bacon.

84
00:02:50.979 --> 00:02:51.850
(gasps)

85
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.090
I love it, I mean--

86
00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.883
Quite a feast. It's quite a feast.

87
00:02:54.883 --> 00:02:56.770
Well, we love Pink's and we're so happy

88
00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:58.043
the Pink's family is back,

89
00:02:58.043 --> 00:03:01.050
and it is going strong opening after the pandemic,

90
00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:03.308
the lines are continuing around the block.

91
00:03:03.308 --> 00:03:04.141
(applause)

92
00:03:04.141 --> 00:03:07.380
Thank you so much!

93
00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.862
A hot dog is not a sandwich.

94
00:03:08.862 --> 00:03:10.278
(laughter)

95
00:03:10.278 --> 00:03:11.480
Thank you for saying it.

96
00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:13.880
Seth, I just can't thank you enough

97
00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.210
for gracing us with your presence.

98
00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:18.600
I'm sure you have a lot of requests.

99
00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:19.433
No, I'm very happy to be here.

100
00:03:19.433 --> 00:03:21.760
But, You know what Seth? I'll say this.

101
00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.682
It ain't no fun without the bun.

102
00:03:23.682 --> 00:03:26.515
(uplifting music)

